Folder\-browser listings, one file per host.
.TP
.IR ~/.cache/claude\-herdr/hosts/ ", " cm/ ", " <agent>\-commands ", " debug.log
The remote herdr path, ssh control sockets, the wrapped agent's subcommand
list (e.g.
.IR claude\-commands )
and the debug log.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/claude\-herdr/history.jsonl
Sessions you started.
Used by
.BR history ,
.B recent
and
.BR last .
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
ssh aliases.
.B "host add"
appends to it, after making a backup.
.TP
.I ~/.config/herdr/config.toml
herdr's configuration.
.B "theme herdr \-\-apply"
edits a marked block in it.
.TP
.I ~/.warp/tab_configs/claude_*.toml
Warp tab configs, written by
.BR shortcuts .
.SH JSON OUTPUT
These shapes are stable; the Raycast extension and
.B self\-update
rely on them.
.TP
.B ls \-\-json
.nf
{version, generated_at, hosts: [{alias, machine, color, address, reachable,
  error, stale, fetched_at, latency_ms, sessions: [{host, name, label, display,
  pane_id, tab_id, workspace_id, terminal_id, agent, status, status_since, cwd,
  title, mark, hue, glyph, color, focused}]}]}
.fi
.TP
.B status \-\-json
.nf
{total, working, blocked, done, idle,
 hosts: [{alias, reachable, sessions, blocked, working}],
 needs_you: [{host, name, display, title}], generated_at}
.fi
.TP
.B host list \-\-json
.nf
[{alias, address, herdr, default, fleet, color}]
.fi
.TP
.B recent \-\-json
.nf
[{host, dir, count, last, score}]
.fi
.TP
.B history \-\-json
.nf
[{t, host, dir, name, agent, args, prompt, worktree}]
.fi
.TP
.B preset ls \-\-json
.nf
[{name, host, dir, args, agent, worktree, prompt}]
.fi
.TP
.B doctor \-\-json
.nf
{ok, warn, fail, sections: [{section, checks: [{status, label, text, fix}]}]}
.fi
.PP
.B status
is one of
.BR working ,
.B blocked
(needs you),
.B done
(finished, not yet seen),
.B idle
or
.BR unknown .
Times are unix seconds.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed: no such session, unreachable host, failed doctor checks,
and so on.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, unknown command, or a command that isn't built yet.
.TP
.B 127
The wrapped agent is needed for a passthrough but isn't installed.
.TP
.B 97
A passthrough was refused
.RB ( CLAUDE_HERDR_NO_PASSTHROUGH ).
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Set up a machine and check everything:
.nf
claude host add b31 selene@10.0.0.49
claude doctor
.fi
.TP
Add a second machine to the dashboard:
.nf
claude host include gpu2
claude
.fi
.TP
Set a new machine up without questions (herdr, Node.js, two agents):
.nf
claude host setup box3 \-\-agents claude,codex \-\-yes
.fi
.TP
Start a session with a first prompt, then four tiled ones from a preset:
.nf
claude new \-\-dir /srv/px \-m "fix the flaky tests"
claude preset add train \-\-host gpu2 \-\-dir /srv/train \-\- \-\-model opus
claude \-\-host gpu2 new @train \-\-tile 4
.fi
.TP
Answer a question and send a follow\-up without attaching:
.nf
claude keys gpu2:ignite 1
claude send ignite "now run the benchmarks"
.fi
.TP
Script against the fleet:
.nf
claude ls \-\-json | jq \-r '.hosts[].sessions[] | select(.status=="blocked") | .host + ":" + .name'
claude status \-\-short          # e.g. in a status bar
.fi
